        "excerpts": [
          "“Obviously I really tried to play my game,\" Bergs said. \"I just felt like last week in Tokyo I really was in good shape, this week in training as well. Just feeling the ball, being aggressive and also serving quite well. The percentages have been really high in the past few matches because we really worked on it, and this gave me a little bit of breathing room. I have a good return, and if I serve well, I can utilise this even more.",
          "Bergs hardly put a foot wrong in his second tour-level meeting with Alcaraz, at least until he served for the match at 5-4 in the second set. Roared on by a Shanghai crowd eager for more action, Alcaraz capitalised on a drop in the 27-year-old Belgian’s level to break serve and force a tie-break."
